"The patient underwent a robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage of pT2c, negative surgical margins, and no invasion of the seminal vesicles. The preoperative PSA was 5.2. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and negative lymphovascular invasion. No lymph nodes were removed, and nodal status is documented as pNx, which widens uncertainty as missing nodal sampling is relevant. Biopsy findings showed a Gleason 3+4 and 3+3 pattern.\n\nFactors driving prognosis include the negative margins and absence of seminal vesicle invasion. Countervailing findings include the preoperative PSA of 5.2 and the pNx nodal status. The prognosis is assessed with a numeric horizon suggesting an expected follow-up without an event. Information that would revise this prognosis significantly includes the postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory. The current uncertainty regarding nodal sampling status must be noted. The fixed estimated horizon is 84.76 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 50.86–118.66 months; its coverage has not been validated."
